{
  "name": "161. Vertex endpoint selection and header forwarding (vertex endpoint fixture)",
  "description": "Local fixture regression, no network traffic leaves the machine. Run tests/e2e/api/runners/vertex-endpoint-fixture.mjs --app-dir <dir>, start an isolated gateway with -app-dir <dir> (the fixture writes its config.json: one Vertex key per region, a service account whose token_uri points at the fixture, and a proxy_config + CA so the gateway trusts the fixture), and run with vertexEndpointFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The fixture is the gateway's HTTP proxy: it terminates TLS for whatever host the gateway CONNECTs to, records the decrypted request, and answers with a canned Gemini or Claude body, so the cases assert the real host, location path segment and headers the gateway sends. Keys are selected with x-bf-api-key. Covered: global, us/eu multi-region, us-east5 regional, a regional key that stays single-region for Gemini, Claude promoted to the us multi-region pool from an unpinned us-central1 key and kept on us-central1 with force_single_region, the OAuth token path for Claude, the service-tier shared-request-type header (global endpoint only, and absent on a regional key), and extra-header forwarding, which is how Vertex Provisioned Throughput spend-limit ids (x-goog-spend-limit-id) are sent. Video retrieve and download pinned to the us-east5 key poll the region named in the operation, us-central1, since model-less polls can land on any key.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "161.1 vertex/gemini-2.5-flash on the global key reaches aiplatform.googleapis.com (vertex endpoint selection)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "vertex-global"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"vertex/gemini-2.5-flash\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"hi\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 8\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('vertexEndpointFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "} else {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: 'http://127.0.0.1:8792/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function () {});",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('the gateway answered from the fixture', function () { pm.expect(j.choices[0].message.content, pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.equal('hello'); });",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: 'http://127.0.0.1:8792/__connects', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('fixture reachable', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); });",
              "  var calls = res.json().data[0].requests.filter(function (q) { return q.method === 'POST' && /:(generateContent|rawPredict)/.test(q.path); });",
              "  pm.test('exactly one prediction call reached Vertex', function () { pm.expect(calls.length, JSON.stringify(calls.map(function (c) { return c.host + c.path; }))).to.equal(1); });",
              "  var call = calls[0] || { host: '', path: '', headers: {}, body: '' };",
              "  var loc = (call.path.match(/locations\\/([^/]+)\\//) || [])[1];",
              "  pm.test('host is aiplatform.googleapis.com', function () { pm.expect(call.host).to.equal('aiplatform.googleapis.com'); });",
              "  pm.test('path location is global', function () { pm.expect(loc, call.path).to.equal('global'); });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
